{
  "order": 24000,
  "name": "Repository routes",
  "kind": "route",
  "responsibility": "Lists the repositories the navigator shows, chooses a repository's checkout for the whole machine, and watches the registry file so every pane follows each change, whoever made it",
  "description": "GET /api/repositories answers under the settings-read browser-origin guard; PUT /api/repositories/chosen {repository, root} answers under the mutation guard, as the opener settings do. Neither names a vault, because the list and the choice belong to the machine. A root that is not a known checkout of the repository is refused (CHECKOUT_UNKNOWN, 404): the page offers nothing else, and the route never registers one. The server watches the registry file from start to stop and follows every change it has not followed yet: the menu's choice, an agent's show or a finished move that chose, a repo command or the first command in a checkout, and another server's show. Then every pane in the vault of a checkout that is not chosen moves to the chosen one, keeping its board, every other pane hears the name its repository goes by now, and every tab hears repositories_changed.",
